 "notes": [
  "All IDs are MusicBrainz MBIDs (UUIDs). They appear in result URLs such as /artist/{mbid}, /release-group/{mbid} and /genre/{mbid}.",
  "Keyword search (/search), tag pages (/tag/...), /recording/... and /area/... pages are disallowed by robots.txt, so this CLI has no search command. Find entities by browsing (list-genres, list-instruments, artist discography) or via known MBIDs.",
  "An intermittent bot check (/__meb_verify, a 'Verifying your browser' page) blocked release detail (/release/{id}), artist tabs (/artist/{id}/releases) and label pages (/label/{id}). Those commands are omitted. If any command returns a page titled 'Verifying your browser', wait and retry.",
  "For heavy or programmatic use, MusicBrainz documents an official JSON web service at https://musicbrainz.org/ws/2/ (e.g. /ws/2/release/{mbid}?inc=recordings&fmt=json). It requires a descriptive User-Agent and allows about 1 request per second. It was not captured in this recording.",
  "Keep request rates low (around 1 per second) to avoid triggering the bot check.",
  "HTML table rows for instrument tabs, release-group releases and country statistics return a 'row' field holding the whole row's text, because the columns cannot be targeted individually."
 ],
